---
import Layout from '../layouts/base.astro'
---
<Layout title="Activities">
  <main id="main" class="page">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <h1>Activities</h1>
      <p class="lede">Practice together, solve challenges, and see what the club has built.</p>
    </header>
    <section id="competitions" class="content-section">
      <h2>Competitions and CTFs</h2>
      <p>Capture the Flag (CTF) competitions are cybersecurity challenges where participants solve problems to find hidden flags. In fall 2024, club teams participated in Hivestorm and the National Cyber League (NCL).</p>
      <p>According to a member's fall 2024 recap, the club fielded four Hivestorm teams and two NCL teams. The NCL teams placed 107th in the experienced bracket and 128th in the standard bracket.</p>
      <p>In November 2025, the club hosted a Murderbot-themed CTF with challenges in OSINT, reconnaissance, web exploitation, forensics, reverse engineering, and cryptography.</p>
      <p class="source">Sources: <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/posts/samielt_cybersecurity-infosec-nmsu-activity-7270163415120121857-XHqR">fall 2024 recap</a> and <a href="https://crimsonconnection.nmsu.edu/event/11834123">2025 CTF listing</a>.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Projects</h2>
      <p>The club's public GitHub includes <a href="https://github.com/NMSU-Cybersecurity-Club/ctf-scripts">scripts for preparing CTF environments</a> and other repositories.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/NMSU-Cybersecurity-Club">Explore the club's GitHub ↗</a></div>
    </section>
    <section id="workshops" class="content-section">
      <h2>Workshops</h2>
      <p>The club's public profile highlights hands-on learning, training, and security challenges. A past password-cracking workshop was listed on February 20, 2025; check with the club for current workshops.</p>
      <p class="source">Source: <a href="https://crimsonconnection.nmsu.edu/event/10911086">2025 workshop listing</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
